RelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000084 \"immature T cell\")\n\n  Line 4611: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000084 \"mature T cell\")\n\n  Line 10925: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000806 \"DN2 immature T cell\")\n\n  Line 10943: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000807 \"DN3 immature T cell\")\n\n  Line 10960: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasExactSynonym obo:CL_0000808 \"DN4 immature T cell\")\n\n  Line 11001: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasRelatedSynonym obo:CL_0000811 \"CD8-positive, alpha-beta immature T cell\")\n\n  Line 11832: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12415312\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000893 \"An immature T cell located in the thymus.\")\n\n  Line 11833: AnnotationAssertion(oboInOwl:hasBroadSynonym obo:CL_0000893 \"immature T cell\")\n\n  Line 12069: AnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:add\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:pam\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:tfm\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GO_REF:0000031\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:18395547\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0000910 \"A mature T cell that differentiated and acquired cytotoxic function with the phenotype perforin-positive and granzyme-B positive.\")\n\n  Line 18515: # Class: obo:CL_0002419 (mature T cell)\n\n  Line 18523: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002419 \"mature T cell\")\n\n  Line 18528: # Class: obo:CL_0002420 (immature T cell)\n\n  Line 18536: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_0002420 \"immature T cell\")\n\n  Line 19236: AnnotationAssertion(rdfs:comment obo:CL_0002489 \"These are precursors to mature T cells; normally, they do not circulate, but are found in the thymus and they have not undergone rearrangement of the alpha and beta T cell receptor genes.\")\n\n\n/home/runner/work/eval-ont-agent-cl/eval-ont-agent-cl/__pr_result__/for_reference/Manchester_CL_normalisation_expt/owl/go.owl:\n  Line 22921:             >The change in morphology and behavior of a mature or immature T cell resulting from exposure to a mitogen, cytokine, chemokine, cellular ligand, or an antigen for which it is specific, leading to the initiation or perpetuation of an immune response.</def>\n\n  Line 23040:             >The change in morphology and behavior of a mature or immature T cell resulting from exposure to an antigen for which its T cell receptor is specific bound to an MHC molecule on an antigen presenting cell, leading to the initiation or perpetuation of an immune response.</def>\n\n  Line 65296:             >A type of T cell apoptosis that occurs towards the end of the expansion phase following the initial activation of mature T cells by antigen and is triggered by T cell receptor stimulation and signals transmitted via various surface-expressed members of the TNF receptor family such as Fas ligand, Fas, and TNF and the p55 and p75 TNF receptors.</def>\n\n  Line 217618:             >immature T cell proliferation</rdfs:label>\n\n  Line 217623:             >The expansion of an immature T cell population by cell division.</def>\n\n  Line 217632:             >immature T cell proliferation in the thymus</rdfs:label>\n\n  Line 217649:             >The expansion of an immature T cell population by cell division in the thymus.</def>\n\n  Line 217704:             >regulation of immature T cell proliferation</rdfs:label>\n\n\n(Results truncated: showing 100 of 295 matches (195 hidden). Consider using a more specific path or pattern.)","metadata":{"matches":295,"truncated":true},"title":"mature T cell","time":{"start":1778517791303,"end":1778517791357}},"id":"prt_e17ebce84001HN0dK4EQPdko0S","sessionID":"ses_1e818387dffedBCC6S3FhFEbCH","messageID":"msg_e17ea2346001VmykvYKlv82vzx"}}
